Changes against the source:

  - Removed: the WebSocket transport (responses_websocket.go, websocket_*.go and
    the github.com/coder/websocket dependency), the image-limit classification
    with internal/domain/image_limits.go, the account-pool fields of the target
    (provider, account, key, generation, route revision, session), hosted tools
    allowed per provider, and the continuation store for previous_response_id:
    a Chat Completions target refuses previous_response_id, and a follow-up
    resends the whole conversation with its reasoning items.
  - Fixed, each with its test: the instructions and the system and developer
    messages join into one first system message in the order of the input;
    reasoning of a model without reasoning is dropped instead of refused, and
    an effort above the profile's highest one (high unless declared) is
    lowered to it; a stream or a response without usage ends normally with
    unknown tokens; a usage whose total disagrees is accepted with the total
    recomputed; a Chat answer cut by its length (or a content filter) ends as
    response.incomplete, never as response.completed; with the profile's flag,
    <think>, <thinking> and ◁think▷ markup leaked into the text goes to the
    reasoning, also when a stream tears a tag; tool_choice reaches a Chat
    provider in its form; a tool output given as an array of items is joined
    into its text; a call_id that comes again keeps both calls and outputs,
    told apart and in order; an HTTP refusal carries the provider's
    Retry-After; the caller sets the request body ceiling (64 MiB unless set)
    and a body over it is refused as request_too_large; the passthrough sends
    the headers the target names instead of a fixed list of ChatGPT headers.
  - Added: the face of the module, package translate at its root (the rest is
    internal/); the target names the provider's model instead of a table of
    model mappings; an error carries at most 4 KiB of the provider's refusal,
    and a refused result no copy of it; the provider's key is replaced in the
    text of a failure (an error, the error of a result and of its
    response.failed event) before that text is cut, while the answer and the
    other events are left as they are; built-in Responses tools and their
    input items are refused before the provider is called, in both protocols.
  - The package is named provider and the module has its own path.

Tests of the source not carried over: the WebSocket tests (22: the three of
responses_interrupt_test.go, the eighteen WebSocket tests of
websocket_*_test.go and TestResponsesWebSocketUsesResponseCreateAndStopsAtTerminal,
with the websocket cases of the shared tests) and the continuation store tests
(2: TestContinuationBoundedLRU, TestVirtualContinuationDoesNotCrossRouteRevision).
TestSSELineBoundBeforeUnboundedAllocation of websocket_sessions_test.go bounds
the SSE reader and is carried over to stream_bound_test.go.
BenchmarkWebSocketRequestPipeline became BenchmarkChatRequestPipeline.
